   "daf": "31b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "הָיָה בָּטֵל מִן הַסֶּלַע, לֹא יֹאמַר לוֹ ״תֵּן לִי סֶלַע״, אֶלָּא נוֹתֵן לוֹ שְׂכָרוֹ כְּפוֹעֵל (בָּטֵל). תְּנַן: נוֹתֵן לוֹ שְׂכָרוֹ כְּפוֹעֵל בָּטֵל.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If in the course of tending to and returning the lost item, the finder «was idle from» labor that would have earned him «a sela, he shall not say to» the owner of the item: «Give me a sela» to compensate me for my lost income. «Rather,» the owner «gives him his wage as» if he were «a laborer.» The Gemara cites that «we learned» in a baraita (Tosefta 4:11): The owner «gives him his wage as» if he were «an idle laborer.»"
  }
 ],
